Engineered an automated end-to-end CI/CD delivery pipeline for a containerized Python Flask microservice using Pytest, Docker, and GitHub Actions.
Upgraded a basic build-test workflow into an enterprise-ready continuous delivery lifecycle by securely managing credentials, executing automated 
unit tests, and publishing multi-tagged, immutable container images directly to Docker Hub upon code merges.

Source Repository:devops-starter-project

This project upgrades a standard build-and-test workflow into a complete Continuous Delivery (CD) pipeline.
 On every push to the main branch, the pipeline verifies code quality with automated unit tests and securely builds, tags, and pushes an immutable Docker image to Docker Hub.

[ Developer Machine ] 
       │ git push origin main
       ▼
[ GitHub Repository ]
       │ Triggers Webhook
       ▼
[ GitHub Actions CI/CD Runner ]
       ├── Job 1: unit-tests (Continuous Integration)
       │     ├── 1. Checkout repository files
       │     ├── 2. Set up Python 3.11 environment
       │     ├── 3. Install requirements (Flask, Pytest)
       │     └── 4. Execute test suite (`python -m pytest`)
       │
       └── Job 2: build-and-package (Continuous Delivery)
             │ (Requires Job 1 to succeed)
             ├── 1. Checkout repository files
             ├── 2. Set up Docker Buildx
             ├── 3. Authenticate to Docker Hub via GitHub Secrets
             └── 4. Build & Push image with multi-tagging:
                   ├── `:latest`
                   └── `:${{ github.sha }}`


